    "answer": {
      "short": "Any pair of exponents whose product is $15$, for example $(1,15)$, $(3,5)$, $(5,3)$ or $(15,1)$, in inner–outer exponent order.",
      "worked": "Let the inner and outer exponents be $a$ and $b$.\n$$\\begin{align*}(2^5)^6&=2^{30}\\\\(4^a)^b&=4^{ab}\\\\&=2^{2ab}\\end{align*}$$\nEqual powers of base $2$ give\n$$\\begin{align*}2ab&=30\\\\ab&=15.\\end{align*}$$\nFor example, the inner–outer pairs $(1,15)$, $(3,5)$, $(5,3)$ and $(15,1)$ all work.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
